  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Shield Logo**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s uploaded image, specifically the logo. The sidebar contains a shield icon with a blue checkmark, and the text \"ASHIELDER\" in bold. Underneath \"ASHIELDER\" is \"SECURE \342\200\242\". I\'m trying to decipher what this visual language is communicating.\n\n\n**Exploring the Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the navigation structure. I\'ve identified the dashboard, investigation (which is currently active), threat intelligence, reports, evidence vault, and settings. The sidebar also features a card with the text \"AI-Powered Email Forensic Intelligence\" and \"Safer Institutions, Stronger India,\" complete with a faint map outline. Moving to the top bar, I see the notification bell, and the avatar section with \"TD\" for Tarun Dange. The main area\'s breadcrumb indicates \"Home > Investigation.\" I noticed a blue pill-shaped \"+ Add Email v\" button.\n\n\n**Defining Email Ingestion Methods**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the email ingestion options. I\'ve broken down the central card into four distinct methods: connecting Gmail (using the Gmail icon), connecting to Microsoft (represented by the Microsoft 4-square icon), uploading an .EML file (depicted by a file icon), and sending an email to a server (signified by a mail icon). Each option offers a concise explanation of its function: importing, integration, drag-and-drop, and forwarding respectively. I\'m noting the visual cues used for each method.\n\n\n"
