  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Visual Context**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the reference image, specifically \"ChatGPT Image Sep 7, 2026, 10_42_29 PM.png\". I\'m meticulously dissecting the visual elements, starting with a close examination of the left sidebar. The logo\'s position is noted as I begin analyzing other elements.\n\n\n**Dissecting the Sidebar**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the sidebar details. The \"ASHIELDER\" logo with its \"SECURE \342\200\242 ANALYSE \342\200\242 PROTECT\" tagline is clear. I am carefully cataloging the menu items, specifically the icons associated with \"Dashboard\", \"Investigation\" (currently active with the search icon), \"Threat Intelligence\", \"Reports\", \"Evidence Vault\", and \"Settings\". I am also noting the light-blue/grey gradient card at the bottom left with the map of India silhouette and text, \"AI-Powered Email Forensic Intelligence\". The background is noted as white.\n\n\n**Confirming the Sidebar Hue**\n\nThe sidebar is undeniably white in the reference image. The \"ASHIELDER\" logo remains at the top, followed by the familiar menu items: Dashboard, Investigation (active), Threat Intelligence, Reports, Evidence Vault, and Settings. The rounded, light-blue card at the bottom with the India map and text confirms the color context. I have identified the clean top header with the bell icon, \"TD\" avatar, and chevron, noting the absence of a search bar.\n\n\n**Examining the Main Content**\n\nI am now focusing on the main content area. I\'ve noted the breadcrumbs \"Home > Investigation,\" the \"Investigation\" title, and its subtitle. I am documenting the blue \"+ Add Email \342\226\276\" button at the top right and am meticulously dissecting the options in the dropdown menu: \"Connect Gmail,\" \"Microsoft Outlook,\" \"Upload .EML File,\" and \"Send Email to Server.\" I\'m also examining the central ingestion area, specifically the large rounded card or container.\n\n\n**Detailing the Ingestion Options**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the main content area\'s central ingestion options. Specifically, I\'m examining the \"Start an Investigation\" heading and its subheading. I\'ve noted the row of four cards, meticulously documenting each icon (Gmail, Microsoft, file, envelope), title, and subtitle, and have started organizing them. I am paying close attention to the visual hierarchy.\n\n\n**Cataloging the Ingestion Area**\n\nI am now completing the detailed documentation of the ingestion area, meticulously noting the \"drop a .eml file here\" instruction, including the clickable \"or browse files\" link. I am also thoroughly cataloging the \"Recent Investigations\" card, the header elements with the clock icon, the \"View All\" link, and all the columns within the table. I\'m focusing on the sample row details, including the status pills, risk scores, and icons.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Table Data**\n\nI\'ve completed cataloging the sample rows within the \"Recent Investigations\" area. I\'m focusing on the details: subject, source, status indicators, and risk scores. I can now provide a detailed summary of the recent investigations. I\'m now transitioning to the existing app\'s structure, focusing on the available routes.\n\n\n\n**Mapping the App Routes**\n\nMy focus has shifted to establishing the precise routing. Based on the reference image and prompt, the investigation page is crucial. I\'ve confirmed `/investigations` is the correct path for the Investigation menu, as indicated by the active state in the image and the breadcrumb trail. The existing app\'s structure guides my next steps.\n\n\n"
