eral options for importing emails. The page\'s header title is \"Investigation\" with a concise subtitle.\n\n\n**Structuring Ingestion Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the ingestion box within the investigation page, specifically \"Start an Investigation.\" It\'s a rounded container with a central badge displaying an envelope icon. This area provides options to begin a new investigation, and I am currently outlining 4 ingestion cards within a grid layout, detailing the connection to Gmail.\n\n\n**Detailing Ingestion Cards**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the ingestion cards. I\'m focusing on the Gmail card, which details \"Import and analyze emails from your inbox,\" featuring a subtle hover effect and detailed text styling. I\'m also planning the Microsoft card, with an authentic 4-color Microsoft icon and the upload card which will feature the ability to drag and drop. All the cards have a consistent look and feel with clear, concise descriptions.\n\n\n**Refining Ingestion UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Send Email to Server\" card, including the mail envelope icon, the descriptive text, and the hover effects. I\'m also adding a divider with the \"or\" text. I\'m then adding a drag and drop section.\n\n\n**Implementing Drag-and-Drop**\n\nI\'ve just added the drag-and-drop feature for `.eml` files. I am now creating the section containing the text \"Drag & drop a .eml file here\" with detailed styling and a hidden file input for browsing. The \"or\" divider is also implemented, along with the \"browse files\" option, and the bottom section featuring recent investigations. The recent investigation section includes the header and table.\n\n\n**Defining Investigation Table**\n\nI\'m now detailing the investigation table. I\'ve designed columns for `Source`, `Status`, `Risk Score`, and `Date`, alongside actions. I\'m focusing on the first two rows, particularly. The first has a malicious status with a high risk, and the second is clean with a low risk, for demonstration. Each row will include actions such as opening cases or analyzing.\n\n\n\n**Designing Investigation Table Rows**\n\nI\'m now detailing the investigation table rows in depth. I\'ve designed a row with \"Invoice #78291,\" marked as suspicious with a risk score of 68 and a yellow status badge. There\'s also an uploaded file (.eml) indicator and consistent \"Actions\" column with three dots. This mimics a dynamic row which would appear at the top.\n\n\n**Constructing Investigation Plan**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Send Email to Server\" card, specifically the inbound SMTP instructions. I\'m focusing on the forwarding address, `analyze-soc@ashielder.targetcorp.in`, and the \"Simulate Inbound SMTP Specimen\" button. I\'m also planning the Forensic Investigation Plan, and the multiple pipeline stages involved. I\'m outlining Target Specimen Details, and various analysis stages, including header analysis, authentication checks, geolocation, and URL evaluation.\n\n\n"
