  planner_response {
    response: "I have built the Primary Investigation Page for Ashielder, delivering an exact visual and functional reproduction of the reference specification.\n\n### Key Highlights\n\n- **Structural Layout & Aesthetic Matching**:\n  - **Sidebar & Branding**: Implemented the Ashielder shield icon with checkmark, the `ASHIELDER` wordmark, and `SECURE \342\200\242 ANALYSE \342\200\242 PROTECT` tagline. Configured navigation with **Investigation** in its active highlight state, and added the bottom card featuring the *\"AI-Powered Email Forensic Intelligence \342\200\242 Safer Institutions \342\200\242 Stronger India\"* banner alongside the vector map silhouette of India.\n  - **Header & Navigation Bar**: Synchronized breadcrumbs (`Home > Investigation`), page title, subtitle (*\"Analyze suspicious emails, trace threats, and uncover the truth.\"*), notification badges, and the analyst profile avatar.\n  - **Action Controls**: Added the primary **`+ Add Email \342\226\276`** dropdown menu featuring options to Connect Gmail, Microsoft, Upload .EML, and Send Email to Server.\n\n- **Forensic Ingestion Hub**:\n  - **Central Ingestion Workspace**: Created the dashed ingestion card centered by the circular envelope badge, subtitle, and the 4-card operational grid (Connect Gmail, Connect Microsoft, Upload .EML File, and Send Email to Server).\n  - **Drag-and-Drop Dropzone**: Implemented the wide dashed drag-and-drop bar supporting RFC 822 `.eml` files with browser-native SHA-256 integrity calculation.\n\n- **INGEST \342\206\222 PLAN \342\206\222 INVESTIGATE \342\206\222 RESULTS Workflow**:\n  - **Ingest**: Select from live mail accounts or upload raw email specimens.\n  - **Plan**: Inspect pre-flight checks, cryptographic SHA-256 hashes, deduplication status, and scheduled analysis execution layers.\n  - **Investigate**: Real-time telemetry monitoring multi-layer execution (MIME parsing, SPF/DKIM/DMARC matrix, hop topology, LightURLNet, and multi-agent synthesis) under the active SLA budget.\n  - **Results**: Immediate verdict display, 2D threat risk score, confidence rating, and direct entry into the full case workspace.\n\n- **Recent Investigations Queue**:\n  - Rendered the forensic cases table mirroring the reference items (*Urgent: Account Verification Required*, *Meeting Schedule - Project Update*, *Invoice #78291*) with risk scores, verdict badges, source icons, dates, and contextual action menus."
    thinking: "**Verifying Components and Features**\n\nOkay, the build\'s complete! I\'m now meticulously visually inspecting the interface. I\'m starting with a detailed QA check. Specifically, I am focusing on the navigation and sidebar elements. So far, the Shield logo, complete with the checkmark, and the \"ASHIELDER\" text, are looking correct. Also, I am verifying the \"SECURE \342\200\242 ANALYSE \342\200\242 PROTECT\" text, which is in uppercase.\n\n\n**Confirming Key Interface Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the core investigation view. The breadcrumb and investigation header look right. I\'m satisfied with the subtitle text. The \"+ Add Email\" button has the proper color and function. The dropdown options, including the icons for Gmail and Microsoft, and the file upload option, are also correct. I think the nav list, with the active investigation, is also correct. The bottom card with \"AI-Powered...\" is great, especially the India map SVG silhouette!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the Primary Investigation Page for Ashielder, delivering an exact visual and functional reproduction of the reference specification.\n\n### Key Highlights\n\n- **Structural Layout & Aesthetic Matching**:\n  - **Sidebar & Branding**: Implemented the Ashielder shield icon with checkmark, the `ASHIELDER` wordmark, and `SECURE \342\200\242 ANALYSE \342\200\242 PROTECT` tagline. Configured navigation with **Investigation** in its active highlight state, and added the bottom card featuring the *\"AI-Powered Email Forensic Intelligence \342\200\242 Safer Institutions \342\200\242 Stronger India\"* banner alongside the vector map silhouette of India.\n  - **Header & Navigation Bar**: Synchronized breadcrumbs (`Home > Investigation`), page title, subtitle (*\"Analyze suspicious emails, trace threats, and uncover the truth.\"*), notification badges, and the analyst profile avatar.\n  - **Action Controls**: Added the primary **`+ Add Email \342\226\276`** dropdown menu featuring options to Connect Gmail, Microsoft, Upload .EML, and Send Email to Server.\n\n- **Forensic Ingestion Hub**:\n  - **Central Ingestion Workspace**: Created the dashed ingestion card centered by the circular envelope badge, subtitle, and the 4-card operational grid (Connect Gmail, Connect Microsoft, Upload .EML File, and Send Email to Server).\n  - **Drag-and-Drop Dropzone**: Implemented the wide dashed drag-and-drop bar supporting RFC 822 `.eml` files with browser-native SHA-256 integrity calculation.\n\n- **INGEST \342\206\222 PLAN \342\206\222 INVESTIGATE \342\206\222 RESULTS Workflow**:\n  - **Ingest**: Select from live mail accounts or upload raw email specimens.\n  - **Plan**: Inspect pre-flight checks, cryptographic SHA-256 hashes, deduplication status, and scheduled analysis execution layers.\n  - **Investigate**: Real-time telemetry monitoring multi-layer execution (MIME parsing, SPF/DKIM/DMARC matrix, hop topology, LightURLNet, and multi-agent synthesis) under the active SLA budget.\n  - **Results**: Immediate verdict display, 2D threat risk score, confidence rating, and direct entry into the full case workspace.\n\n- **Recent Investigations Queue**:\n  - Rendered the forensic cases table mirroring the reference items (*Urgent: Account Verification Required*, *Meeting Schedule - Project Update*, *Invoice #78291*) with risk scores, verdict badges, source icons, dates, and contextual action menus."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 431807517
    }
