  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Ashielder Logo**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `AshielderLogo` component in `src/components/ui/AshielderLogo.tsx`. It\'s the official Ashielder brand logo, which is quite detailed. I\'ve noted the 3D shield emblem, orbital nodes (blue, saffron orange, green, and royal blue), outer ring, concentric background disk, and a centered white checkmark. Now I\'m moving on to details, like how it is rendered.\n\n\n**Revisiting Logo Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on incorporating the old logo elements, specifically the \"A\" with \"SHIELDER\" wordmark, the tricolor accent bar, and the tagline \"FEASIBLE & VIABLE.\" I\'m looking at how these elements can be added back and blend with the existing UI in both light and dark modes. I\'ve noted that `AshielderLogo.tsx` already handles theme variations with `theme={ui.theme}`. The size options also look good.\n\n\n**Verifying Color Contrast**\n\nI\'m now carefully checking the color contrast in `AshielderLogo.tsx` between the light and dark themes. Specifically, I\'m verifying that the white background gradient stops in the radial gradient (lines 40-70) and the wordmark\'s text colors in the light and dark modes blend cleanly. I\'m focusing on lines 40-70 and the wordmark, using Tailwind classes to ensure proper background and text color assignments.\n\n\n**Investigating Tagline Variations**\n\nI\'m now determining if the user can customize the tagline in `AshielderLogo.tsx`. I\'ve confirmed `AshielderLogo`\'s props, including `size`, `variant`, `theme`, and `className`, but none appear to be dedicated to the tagline. The default tagline is \"FEASIBLE & VIABLE\" when `variant=\"full\"`. I am now investigating how this can be modified. I\'m also looking into potential ID conflicts for the radial gradients, especially if the logo is used multiple times. I\'m focusing on the ID attributes for the SVG elements.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 333919685
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
