  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the visual elements of the reference image. The blue shield and white \'A\' are the core components of the logo, and the wordmark \"ASHIELDER\" is clear. I\'m focusing on how to translate these elements for new logo and icon designs, with an eye toward modern aesthetics. I\'m considering variations.\n\n\n**Analyzing the New Details**\n\nI\'ve just refined my approach by noting the tagline and color palette. It seems the exact hex codes are important, and I need to consider 24x24px icons with a 2px stroke, which Lucide icons seem ideal for. The primary logo component I\'ll update is `src/components/ui/AshielderLogo.tsx`, and I\'ll focus on replacing the complex 3D shield with a flat, modern blue shield outline with a white \'A\'.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Core Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise details of the shield and \'A\'. I\'ve clarified the blue is a solid `#0EA5E9` and the \'A\' is white. I\'m building it up in my mind, the outer shield, the inner \'A\' or cut-out within the blue shield. My priority is to create an accurate SVG, initially focusing on a simple `<path>` for the shield and a `<text>` or path for the \'A\', or better I will use SVG paths to draw the shield.\n\n\n**Constructing the SVG**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the SVG. I\'ve got the standard Lucide shield path in mind, and I\'m aiming for an outer outline with an inner solid shield and a white \'A\'. The wordmark \"ASHIELDER\" in a bold sans-serif is also clear, along with the tagline \"Email Threats \342\200\242 Intelligence \342\200\242 Safer Tomorrow\" in a lighter font. I will update `AshielderLogo.tsx` with these changes.\n\n**Reviewing the Updated Colors**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the brand palette. I\'ve noted down the exact hex codes for primary blue (`#0EA5E9`), success (`#10C98A`), warning (`#FFB800`), danger (`#FF365C`), and info (`#8EA0B5`). The blue matches Tailwind\'s `sky-500`. I will adjust the colours in all the components to match this. I will also be updating the component to include the updated tagline.\n\n\n**Refining the Shield\'s Path**\n\nI\'m now refining the SVG path for the shield, specifically focusing on its top edge. It seems straight, not curved, based on the reference images. I\'m aiming for a path that accurately reflects the logo\'s clean, modern aesthetic, particularly the \"08. Logo Usage\" image. I\'ll make a custom path that will match the look perfectly. My goal is to get this detail spot-on for the SVG implementation. I\'ll need to remove the tricolor bar as well, and consider the inverted white/dark color usage.\n\n\n**Implementing the SVG**\n\nI\'m now building the SVG structure based on the reference images, specifically \"01. Brand Logo\". I\'m focusing on a thin, blue outer stroke, a white gap, and a solid blue inner shield with a white \'A\' cutout. I\'ve drafted an SVG structure with `<path>` elements and am refining the shield\'s top edge to match the crest shape. I\'m testing the outline now.\n\n```xml\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <!-- Outer Shield -->\n  <path d=\"M50 95C50 95 10 75 10 40V10L50 5L90 10V40C90 75 50 95 50 95Z\" stroke=\"#0EA5E9\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <!-- Inner Shield -->\n  <path d=\"M50 82C50 82 22 66 22 42V19L50 15L78 19V42C78 66 50 82 50 82Z\" fill=\"#0EA5E9\"/>\n  <!-- Letter A -->\n  <path d=\"M50 30L35 65H43L46 55H54L57 65H65L50 30ZM48 45L50 38L52 45H48Z\" fill=\"white\"/>\n</svg>\n```\nI am now building an SVG structure based on the reference images. I\'m refining the outer shield path to have a crest shape (a V notch at the top), then a white gap, then the solid inner shield and the white A. This will be an accurate representation.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Logo Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Lucide shield path into `AshielderLogo.tsx`, scaling it to fit the design. My previous plan to customize the path is being revised to prioritize