  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to seamlessly integrate the provided logo and icons into the existing system. The challenge is to preserve the integrity of the \"SHIELDER\" and its tricolor bar while ensuring a cohesive visual experience. The second uploaded component needs to be maintained as-is, which adds another layer to consider.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'ve realized the uploaded images\' order is crucial; the screenshot is the second image, not the first. \"Keep it as is\" must mean the tricolor bar and wordmark styling within the system should match the screenshot exactly. Now I need to reconcile that with the design system, which features a different shield logo, icons, and wordmark. It is a matter of integrating two opposing style guides.\n\n\n**Reconciling Visual Styles**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of visual reconciliation. It looks like I need to keep the \"A SHIELDER\" wordmark (blue A) and the tricolor bar from the screenshot but integrate those elements with the existing design system. The user wants the ShieldEmblemSvg to match the design system, as well as the tagline, however, the existing wordmark and the bar must be kept. As for icons, the design system uses lucide-react, but the screenshot has custom icons. Instead of replacing every icon, I\'ll need to figure out how to blend those custom icons in or use lucide-react ones.\n\n\n**Mapping Icon Associations**\n\nI\'ve been mapping the custom icons from the screenshot to their `lucide-react` equivalents. I\'ve successfully associated a suite of icons, like Zap for Lightning Bolt, Mail for Email, and Globe for Domain. I\'m noting the existing design system uses lucide-react with `strokeWidth={2}`. The shield shape is clear, so I\'m investigating what ShieldEmblemSvg entails.\n\n\n**Defining Shield Components**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the ShieldEmblemSvg composition, meticulously deconstructing it to create an accurate recreation. The Design System\'s \"Brand Logo\" reveals a nuanced structure with a Primary Blue outer border, a transparent gap, and a solid Primary Blue \'A\' within. I\'m taking the Dark Background variation into account. I\'m planning to make a shield with a thick stroke and primary blue fill, and a solid \'A\' in the center.\n\n\n**Constructing Shield SVG**\n\nI\'m now implementing the SVG for the Design System shield and making it a key component. I\'m taking the \"08. Logo Usage (Do\'s & Don\'ts)\" into account and the overall flat design. The goal is a shield with a thick stroke and primary blue fill, with an \'A\' inside, with a flat top and a horizontal crossbar. Furthermore, I\'ll update `AshielderLogo.tsx`, keeping the wordmark and tricolor bar, replacing the 3D shield, and updating the tagline to the one in \"10. Tagline & Brand Message.\"\n\n\n**Refining Shield Shape**\n\nOkay, the shield shape needs some fine-tuning. I realized the image\'s shield top is straight and horizontal. After looking at the \"01. Brand Logo\" in more detail, it actually has rounded corners on the horizontal top and the \'A\' inside has a flat top. The Lucide shield is a standard shield. I\'ll need to use a custom SVG for this. Now I\'m preparing to create the SVG!\n\n```xml\n<path d=\"M4 4h16v7c0 6-8 11-8 11s-8-5-8-11V4z\" />\n```\n\n\n**Revising Shield Elements**\n\nI\'ve just recognized a critical detail: the \'A\' within the shield in the design system logo (image 1) is a solid fill, not an outline. Looking at the \"08. Logo Usage (Do\'s & Don\'ts)\", the \"correct\" usage shows the outer shield and the \'A\' inside as blue on a light background. However, on the dark background variation, the A inside is a solid white!\n\n\n**Crafting Shield Variations**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the shield SVG, focusing on matching both light and dark theme variations. I\'m focusing on getting the right styling for the \'A\', and its flat top. I\'m taking the Dark Background variation into account. I\'ve updated the dark theme\'s \'A\' to white, with the border being blue, and the light theme\'s \'A\' to dark blue. Now I\'m refining the SVG paths for the \'A\' to use a polygon fill instead of lines and strokes.\n\n\n**Finalizing Shield Geometry**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the shield shape, and I\'ve found a balanced polygon fill for the flat-top \'A\'. My focus is on the dark and light variations using the `theme` variable. I have finalized the paths for a perfectly filled flat-top \'A\' with balanced dimensions. Now I have a fully functional design system!\n\n```xml\n<path d=\"M15 18 H85 V45 C85 75 50 92 50 92 C50 92 15 75 15 45 Z\" stroke=\"#0EA5E9\" strokeWidth=\"8\" strokeLinejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<path d=\"M46 32 L33 70 H43 L46 60 H54 L57 70 H67 L54 32 H46 Z M48 52 L50 42 L52 52 H48 Z\" fill={theme === \'dark\' ? \'#FFFFFF\' : \'#0B1F33\'} />\n```\n\n\n**Refining \'A\' Element**\n\nI\'m now iterating on refining the \'A\' element within the shield. I\'m focusing on the best way to render the flat top of the \'A\' and I am realizing that strokes won\'t work perfectly. After exploring different approaches, I\'m now crafting a polygon fill for the \'A\', which will provide crisp, clean edges for the flat top, and I am now refining the coordinate paths.\n\n\n**Validating Shape Coordinates**\n\nI\'m now validating the precise SVG coordinates for the flat-top \'A\' and the shield. I\'ve meticulously refined the polygon paths. The goal is to accurately render the A\'s flat top, ensuring crispness across both light and dark themes. The shape now perfectly matches the design system.\n\n\n\n**Updating Tagline Implementation**\n\nI\'m now changing the tagline to \"Email Threats \342\200\242 Intelligence \342\200\242 Safer Tomorrow\" as that came from the design system, and the user wanted the second image to be kept as is. My previous implementation had a slightly different tagline. This change ensures consistency with the overall design, after evaluating the intent of the \"keep as is\" prompt.\n\n\n**Implementing Icon Alignment**\n\nI\'m now implementing the icon alignment strategy, starting with the `lucide-react` library. The intent is to align all design elements. I\'m focusing on \"05. Core Icon Library (24x24px, 2px stroke)\" to ensure consistency. Following the analysis, I\'m replacing the custom icons in the screenshot with their corresponding `lucide-react` equivalents. I\'m going through the list and implementing them.\n\n\n**Mapping Icon Library**\n\nI\'m now mapping the screenshot icons to the `lucide-react` library. My objective is to align all design elements. I\'ve focused on size and stroke width using \"05. Core Icon Library (24x24px, 2px stroke)\" for consistency. I\'m choosing icons like `File` for FileBox, `Clock` for Timeline and `FileBarChart` for Reports. The rest of the list are good too. I\'ll scan the existing system and blend them.\n\n\n"
