    thinking: "**Verifying the Rendering**\n\nI\'ve confirmed there are no TypeScript errors. Now, I\'m meticulously checking the `AshielderLogo.tsx` component\'s rendering. Specifically, I\'m focusing on color accuracy: the outer shield\'s stroke (#0EA5E9), and the \'A\' (white on dark, `#0B1F33` on light). Also, I\'m making sure the wordmark \'A\' is correct.\n\n\n**Analyzing the New Details**\n\nI\'ve incorporated the new color scheme: `#0284c7` for the \"A\" and white for \"SHIELDER\" in the wordmark, mirroring the screenshot. The tricolor bar (Saffron, White, Green) and the tagline are also in place. I\'ve re-reviewed the `ShieldEmblemSvg` code, ensuring it renders the new colors correctly.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Transparency**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \'A\' symbol, specifically the inner cutout. I realized it needs to be transparent. I\'m investigating how the `fill-rule=\"evenodd\"` attribute would affect the rendering of this shape, given its counter-clockwise path. The default `nonzero` fill rule is being overridden in my thoughts, as the path\'s direction has been identified. I am considering `fill-rule=\"evenodd\"`, as this will produce the transparency effect required.\n\n\n**Confirming the Fill Rule**\n\nI\'ve just verified that a clockwise inner path within the counter-clockwise outer path automatically creates a transparent hole, thanks to the `nonzero` fill rule. The inner path, with points (45,49), (50,34), and (55,49), punches a hole. I\'ve also done a quick verification of the \'A\' shape, to make sure it renders correctly.\n\n\n**Refining the \'A\' Shape**\n\nI\'m focused on ensuring the \'A\' symbol renders precisely. I\'m checking the calculations, particularly the crossbar position at Y=58. The outer left X position calculates to approximately 34.2, and the inner left to 43.2. I\'ve re-examined the design system\'s colors, focusing on the discrepancy between the primary blue and the wordmark \'A\'. The colors should align to maintain consistency.\n\n\n**Updating the Sidebar Icons**\n\nI\'m now adapting the icons in `Sidebar.tsx`. I\'ve analyzed the design system\'s icons, and am updating them accordingly. For \"Dashboard,\" I\'m keeping `ShieldAlert`, as it perfectly matches the vertical line and dot within a shield. \"Investigation\" will stay as `Search`. \"Threat Intelligence\" will use `Globe`, matching the design system. I\'m also reviewing `strokeWidth` and adjusting to reflect any necessary visual weight, which may be different, now.\n\n\n**Revising the Sidebar Icons**\n\nI\'m revisiting the sidebar icon choices. I decided to switch \"Threat Intelligence\" from `Globe` to `Database`. For \"Reports,\" I considered `LineChart`, and also considered `BarChart2`, but went with `LineChart` because it felt the best. I\'m keeping \"Evidence Vault\" at `Archive` since it closely aligns with the intended visual. And, finally, I\'ve confirmed that \"Settings\" will use the default `Settings` icon.\n\n\n"
