  planner_response {
    response: "I have fixed the issue causing the React missing key warning in the `ThreatWorldMap` component. \n\n**What was wrong:**\nThe global map was parsing country shapes from the local `worldMapData.json` file and using the `id` field as the React list key (`key={c.id}`). However, a few specific territories (like Somaliland and Kosovo) were mapped in the data without an `id` field, which resulted in `undefined` keys and triggered the console error during rendering.\n\n**What was changed:**\nI updated the SVG rendering loop in `src/features/dashboard/ThreatWorldMap.tsx` to provide a robust fallback chain for the `key` prop:\n```tsx\nkey={c.id || c.name || `country-${i}`}\n```\nThis ensures every single country path receives a guaranteed unique identifier, clearing the React rendering errors seamlessly. The application is building perfectly!"
    modified_response: "I have fixed the issue causing the React missing key warning in the `ThreatWorldMap` component. \n\n**What was wrong:**\nThe global map was parsing country shapes from the local `worldMapData.json` file and using the `id` field as the React list key (`key={c.id}`). However, a few specific territories (like Somaliland and Kosovo) were mapped in the data without an `id` field, which resulted in `undefined` keys and triggered the console error during rendering.\n\n**What was changed:**\nI updated the SVG rendering loop in `src/features/dashboard/ThreatWorldMap.tsx` to provide a robust fallback chain for the `key` prop:\n```tsx\nkey={c.id || c.name || `country-${i}`}\n```\nThis ensures every single country path receives a guaranteed unique identifier, clearing the React rendering errors seamlessly. The application is building perfectly!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
