  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining UX Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve been reviewing the UX improvements, specifically focusing on the toast notification feature within `CaseDetailPage.tsx`. Lines 228-235 highlight the \"Additional options\" button, which triggers the toast. I\'m considering refining the text of the notification message for clarity and brevity. The goal is to make these helpful features obvious.\n\n\n**Rethinking Action Trigger**\n\nI\'m now ditching the toast notification idea, and pushing for a proper dropdown menu triggered by the \"More Actions\" button. The primary focus for this change is the selected UI element, using the CSS selector provided.\n\n\n**Refining Sidebar Interaction**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the sidebar, specifically the Ashielder brand header, to fix the 3-dot menu. The objective is to make the 3-dot interaction functional, since the user is having issues, focusing changes directly on the selected element within `Sidebar.tsx`, and ensuring the styles and behavior are correctly applied. The goal is to make the menu responsive.\n\n\n**Reimagining Dot Interaction**\n\nI\'m now completely rethinking the \"3-dot\" interaction. Initially, I was looking at the 3-dot menu and Ashielder brand header, but it\'s more than a styling fix. The user may interpret the tricolor segments as clickable dots. I propose making these segments interactive, linking them to a workspace/quick navigation menu via tooltip. The code in `AshielderLogo.tsx` is perfect for this, the goal is to make these elements directly functional.\n\n\n**Integrating Header Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating header actions. I\'m considering unifying interaction with both the tricolor bar and the existing \"3-dots\" button, making either trigger a full-featured dropdown. I\'m also looking into handling clicks on the tagline, since it could be confusing. I\'m focusing on unifying the user experience in the header.\n\n\n**Defining Menu Display**\n\nNow, I\'m defining the content for the sidebar dropdown menu, considering distinct sections: header with status, quick navigation links (Overview, Inbox, Investigation, Hunting, Evidence, Reports), workspace partitions, and quick actions, like System Health and mode toggles. I\'m focusing on providing users with a comprehensive set of options. I will next look at the menu\'s implementation using `Sidebar.tsx`.\n\n\n**Verifying Icon Availability**\n\nI\'m now making sure the necessary icons are available in `lucide-react` such as `MoreVertical` and `MoreHorizontal`, since they will be needed for my current work on the sidebar. I\'m also confirming that the component `AshielderLogo.tsx` provides the base structure to start with.\n\n\n**Improving Dot Clarity**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual representation of the tricolor dots within `AshielderLogo.tsx`, transitioning them from segments to distinct, rounded pills with a small gap to improve clarity. These three pills will match the screenshot. I\'m focusing on ensuring these pills trigger the `onDotsClick` event. I will next look at the sidebar.\n\n```\n```\n\n**Implementing Navigation Links**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating navigation links into the sidebar. I will focus on linking the \"Ashielder\" logo and the dedicated \"3-dots\" button to the same dropdown menu. I will make sure the navigation target is the `/overview` route. My current work is focusing on integrating the functionality in `Sidebar.tsx`.\n\n\n\n**Designing Menu Behavior**\n\nI\'m now designing the behavior of the new dropdown menu. I\'ll implement click-outside and escape key listeners to make the interaction intuitive, including a smooth dropdown animation. The menu will feature a tenant/organization section and quick action links like \"Security Overview\", \"New Ingest\", and \"Case Inbox\". It will also have theme mode switch and system status indicator, based on my previous work on `Sidebar.tsx`.\n\n\n**Examining MoreHorizontal Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `MoreHorizontal` icon within `CaseTableRow.tsx` to align with the design updates. Specifically, I\'m analyzing lines 245-266 for the integration of the \"More row actions\" button. My focus is ensuring the existing function of the button is preserved while the design improvements are applied. I am using all systems available.\n\n\n"
